more_label: Lyrics    
    
--more  
[Verse 1]  
We circled 'round the same line, trying to find the thread,  
Words kept slipping through our fingers, left unsaid.  
You laughed, said “turn it into a song,” like you could see the beat,  
I froze, said “buddy, you are on,” and stumbled on my feet.  
  
[Chorus]  
Hey, sing it back, rewind the moment slow,  
Turn the “almost” into music, let the feelings show.  
We missed the cue but found the groove, improvised and bright,  
Buddy, you are on — we’ll sing it through the night.  
  
[Verse 2]  
Coffee-cup confessions, half-remembered plans,  
A tangent turned to chorus in the spaces of our hands.  
You winked, I grabbed the melody, patched the pause with rhyme,  
Two voices finding rhythm in the margin of the time.  
  
[Chorus]  
Hey, sing it back, rewind the moment slow,  
Turn the “almost” into music, let the feelings show.  
We missed the cue but found the groove, improvised and bright,  
Buddy, you are on — we’ll sing it through the night.  
  
[Bridge]  
Loop it once, loop it twice, let the memory bend,  
Every near-miss is a verse if you invite it in.  
We’ll hum the what-if’s louder, make the silence sway,  
When you say “turn it into song,” I’ll never walk away.  
  
[Chorus (fade)]  
Hey, sing it back, rewind the moment slow,  
Turn the “almost” into music, let the feelings show.  
We missed the cue but found the groove, improvised and bright,  
Buddy, you are on — we’ll sing it through the night.  
  
[outro -mechanical robotic spoken voice]  
Want a different style (hip-hop, country, ballad) or to tweak lines?  
Sigh  
--more    
